    4. Populate the second half with its own independent content pattern (same color, different arrangement) — content in each half should occupy different rows [observed]
    5. Choose which half the output is (first or second) and place 2 marker pixels (color=5) in that half on a grid boundary edge, same row or same col, gap=2, at positions that are bg in the output
    6. Return the full grid as input; the output is the half from step 2
